<!-- Bill allocations for the opt-in ageing schedule on tally_get_outstanding.

     Shape copied from day-book-trading.xml, whose BILLALLOCATIONS.LIST came
     from a real export; all values here are invented. Period covered is
     1-Apr-2026 to 31-Jul-2026, and every case is dated so that ageing as at
     31-Jul-2026 lands in a known bucket.

     Bramley (Sundry Creditors) — payables, so bills arrive POSITIVE:
       B-1        raised 01-Apr, 100000, open        -> 121 days, "90+ days"
       B-3        raised 10-Jul,  30000, open        ->  21 days, "0-30 days"
       B-2        raised 01-Jul,  50000, paid 15-Jul -> nets to zero, settled
       B-4        raised 05-Jul,  10000, paid 12000  -> net reverses, overSettled
       B-OLD-99   settlement only, no raising alloc  -> earlier-bill settlement
       (no ref)   On Account allocation              -> unreferenced

     Northwind Retail Limited (Sundry Debtors) — receivables, so the bill
     arrives NEGATIVE. This is the case that matters most: an open receivable
     and an over-settled payable have the same sign, so anything judging
     outstanding-ness by sign alone gets one of them wrong.
       S-9        raised 05-Jul, -20000, open        ->  26 days, "0-30 days" -->
